PANDORAN SLAVERY

Overview & Societal Justification
   When the first Matron Mother to settle Pandora set out from Earth, she did so as the ruler of a small north-Atlantic island nation with her small cadre of 299 colonists, including 38 True Futanari, 40 Intersex or other Futanari, 120 Males, 100 Females, and one 19 year old Futanari Breeder daughter. These weren't slaves, these were friends, lovers, family, and dedicated loyalists, and they weren't going to another world to create a Futanari Supremacy, they were going to found a new & better world where the raping of the planet & exploitation of the poor weren't a facet of life. Their first years on Pandora, and the loss of almost 70 people out of the original 300 had a profound effect on these idealistic settlers and led to a more pragmatic world view. Later, as other Matrons joined the colony, adding their own people and their own ideals to the future of the colony, this pragmatism eroded their idealism bit by bit.
   When pirates attacked a House Singh exploration ship only 2 jumps from Pandora in early 2294, and House Singh was able to capture the ship at great cost & a bit of luck, the colony was forced to face several facts. The first was that they were not as alone & isolated as they had thought, the second was that they were not prepared to fight off the threats they were likely to face, and third that they would have to expand their colony much faster than they had planned. So the decision was made to turn these, and all captured prisoners into slaves that could help the colony expand much faster.
   In the years that followed more ships were captured, other matrons joined the colony with their own ideas for the future, and more slaves were added to the colony. Somewhere along the line in the over 2 decades since, slavery went from an uncomfortable necessity to a vital industry. While still looking to build a new & better world where the raping of the planet & exploitation of the poor were a central focus, alongside of that the marginalization of males, institutional social stratification, and the development of a military oligarchy. While there are members of the council that find these developments unpalatable, none have fought against the developments either, and all of them have benefited greatly.
   In the early years of slavery on Pandora, the slaves weren't  really thought of as 'slaves' in the traditional sense, but more like working prisoners. While some of these prisoners were claimed as breeding stock for the Matron Mothers, none were bought or sold, and almost all of the slaves were assigned to work farms. After House Singh captured a large colony ship with over 400 colonists, including many children, the council was forced to make a choice between defining these people, that weren't hostile to them, as working prisoners or giving up all pretense and make slavery official. So in late 2295, the Council of Matrons made slavery legal & official in the Colonial Charter.
   With the influx of additional, unpaid, workers the colony was able to expand much faster, the Matron Mothers were able to expand the population much faster, and many more citizens were able to focus on the construction, engineering, and technical fields. As more slaves were added the face of scientific development increased, more land was able to be cleared for development, and the colonies small fleet of converted jumpships were able to be upgraded with more lethal armaments. At the same time, more and more citizens wanted to own slaves themselves, so slave markets developed to which a small percentage of all new slaves were diverted for purchase by normal citizens. With the private ownership of slaves came slave brothels to satiate the desires of mostly True Futanari who could not afford to purchase a slave, but had enough free money to 'rent' one for a short period. In just a little over 20 years after that first group of pirates was captured, the entire trajectory of the colony had totally changed.

Slave Procurement & Processing
   At the core of the slave trade for the colony are a number of jumpships that have been converted into heavily armed 'raiders'. Some of these ships were lightly armed colony ships before conversion, and others were more heavily armed pirate ships, but all of them have been upgraded with the best weapons and defenses the colony can afford at the moment. All-in-all each of these converted warships are more than a match for almost anything in the uncharted regions of space, and with each carrying a platoon of heavily armed & armored space marines, they have had little real challenge when facing other ships in space. The real challenges the colony has faced has been when capturing other colonies, with hundreds of armed colonists. These raids have required a great degree of coordination between many raider ships, and hundreds of highly trained soldiers, but have netted more slaves in total than all the slaves gained from ships in space. Either way, the whole process of gaining new slaves begins with winning a fight.
   While great care is taken to use non-lethal force against individuals in battle, it is inevitable that some potential slaves are killed in the fight. Those who survive are rounded up, shackled, and inventoried by a Sister of Black who quickly give each slave a preliminary rating that will determine how they are housed & treated on the journey back to Pandora. In this evaluation they will be given one of three ratings based on a number of factors known only to the Sisters of Black, but generally go something like this:
      A. Exceptionally well-trained or educated individuals, exceptionally attractive people, and children.
      B. Most scientists, engineers, doctors, medics, soldiers, craftsmen, technicians, professionals, and teenagers.
      C. Everyone else
Those that fall into group 1 are taken to a secure section of the ship and are off-limits to the crew, but don't receive any further special treatment. Those that fall into group 2 are taken to a larger holding area, and put into cages. The crew may interact with those in this group but are instructed to be gentle if they do. Those who fall into group 3 are taken to the cargo hold and put into cages, and the crew is free to do with them as they wish (within limits like no damage to the merchandise). All captives, no matter what group they are put into, are fed, have their wounds tended, and are given blankets to sleep with. They are also given a chance to refresh themselves when needed under supervision. Most importantly, all are given control collars that monitor their vitals and can provide correctional measures to those who cause problems. During the voyage back to Pandora, the Sister of Black overseeing this collection of slaves will interview and evaluate each captive individually, one-by-one, to more accurately rate each slave for processing back at the colony when they arrive.
   When the raiding ship arrives at Pandora the captives are shuttled down to the colony in small groups, aboard specially equipped slave shuttles operated by the Sisters of Black. These shuttles restrain each captive in individual coffin-like pods and a gas is pumped into the pods to sedate them for the trip. On the ground, each captive is transported, while remaining in the pod, to the nearby slave processing facility and then to an individual secure cell where they will remain for anywhere between a week up to  3 months depending on the number of captives being processed at once. During this period the Ministry of Corrections interviews & evaluates each captive extensively, and forces the captives to undertake a bewildering number of tests to test their physical strength, their agility, their stamina & toughness, their intelligence, their willfulness, their intuitiveness, and their genetics. For some few, a special characteristic revealed during this period will move them out of the normal processing that would follow, but most will be evaluated and transferred to the next phase of processing at the hands of the Sisters of Black.
   Breaking & Training Phase: Once the Ministry of Corrections have finished with their intermediate evaluations, captives are physically moved again, to another facility several kilometers away, to a location known as 'The Obsidian Citadel" for their breaking & training. 
   During the breaking phase of a captive's processing, the Dominas use a combination of pain, pleasure, and sexual humiliation to completely annihilate the captive's spirit. Through the combined use of psychological manipulation, physical torture, private and public humiliation, and systematic sexual abuse, the soon-to-be slaves are broken down and shown that they are utterly powerless. They are shown that not only do they lack control over their lives, but they also lack the power to control their own minds or bodies.
   While much of this is done with traditional techniques used for millennia, what makes the Dominas especially effective are three key pillars of control:
      A. The Voice: All Dominas possess a psionic ability that allows them to give vocal commands backed by psychic influence. While the relative strength and skill of each Domina differs, those who fail to resist its influence are compelled to obey, no matter how extreme the command or how much they might wish to do otherwise.
      B. Bodily Fluids: All Dominas produce bodily fluids that, when ingested by another, exponentially increase physical sensation for a short time. While potency varies, even the least potent can turn a paper cut into the sensation of a dull blade slicing the skin. Dominas with high potency can make a powerful man weep in pain from a simple pinch, or reach an unwanted orgasm from just a warm breath.
      C. The Neurolash: Dominas are trained from childhood in only two weapons: their own bodies and the Neurolash. The Neurolash is a highly versatile tool and weapon that utilizes a variety of energies to cause pain, pleasure, repulsion, attraction, shocks, or extreme temperatures. When used in combination with the Dominas' bodily fluids, most captives break in a remarkably short period.
   Near the culmination of a slave's breaking, when the Domina deems the captive on the brink of total collapse, the subject is repeatedly violated in the most humiliating ways. They are compelled to actively and willingly participate in this process while being observed by those they love or respect—an act designed to sever their final ties to their former identity.
Once a captive is utterly broken, they are handed over to junior members and Ministry staff for Integration Training. During this phase, the captive is instructed on their behavioral expectations, social hierarchies, and the specific labor skills required for their assignment.
   Most importantly, they are taught The Protocol: how to exist within a world where every second of their life is choreographed by the Ministry’s Oversight AI. Because the Sovereign Hand relies on automated management, a slave must learn that an AI command is not a suggestion, but a sequence of mandatory rituals.
   Once the captive has completed their training they officially become a slave and where they go from here depends on how they were categorized during testing. Those that score the highest in this process are generally claimed by the Captain of the ship that captured them, and the controlling owner of the ship that captured them, in a sort of spoils of war claiming right. In this system the Captain of the ship has the right to first pick out of all the slaves captured, and the Owner gets the next two picks of her choice. Generally these picks will be for the highest tier males, who will become breeding slaves to their owner. 

The Ministry of Corrections
   The Sovereign Hand: While there are hundreds of civilians that work in the Ministry of Corrections as guards, scientists, psychologists, child caretakers, and trainers, the most visible symbol of the Ministry as well as those who perform its most core duties, are members of The Sovereign Hand. These women, commonly know as the "Sisters of the Black" due to their uniform and mysterious aura, are elite agents of the Matrons Council as well as highly trained slave breaker. There are currently 105 True Futanari members of the Sisters of the Black that were all originally colonists from House Medina. Those 105 Sisters of the Black were out of 180 that first began forming the organization. Another 19 failed the training to become breeding stock for the next generation, another 40 died during the process, and 16 exited the program early in the training to help their house. Over the 19 years since the failed sisters have given birth to around 200 children, of which 20 were True Futanari, and only 10 of those entered the Sisters of the Black training program. Thus far, only 1 of these children has graduated and become a full fledged member of the order herself. Another 28 children from House Medina have been chosen for the Sisters of Black, but they are all age 16 and below.
   The life of a child within the Sovereign Hand training program is brutal, with near constant physical, emotional, and intellectual stress-testing. As an infant or young child they are  assigned a nanny that becomes their foster mother until shortly after they hit puberty. At age 3 they begin training, with an intensive physical & mental education that involves a great deal of competition for placement in standings. 
   From ages 3-8 these children their education is a balancing act between treating them as children while also preparing them for what will come later. While they still reside with their foster mothers, their days are partitioned into strict blocks of Cognitive Loading and Kinetic Foundations. In the classroom, 'normal' subjects like linguistics and mathematics are taught through the lens of the Ministry, where the children learn to process information at a speed that would break a civilian child. A few key points of this education & training are:
      A. Reactive Instinct. They are taught to move, fall, and strike in synchronized 'Play-Forms' that are secretly designed to build the muscle memory required for the Neurolash.
      B. Agility & Flexibility: Intense gymnastics and martial arts like Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu & Silat are taught. The goal is to maximize the power-to-weight ratio and teach the children how to use an opponent’s momentum against them.
      C. Cognitive Scoping or Environmental Processing. The children are trained to develop near-eidetic recall through high-speed visualization drills. Utilizing "Kim’s Game" variants and rapid-exposure "Flash-Coding," they learn to enter a room and instantly inventory every exit, weapon, and biometric tell of the occupants. By age 8, their brains are conditioned to "archive" a scene in a single glance, allowing them to provide detailed intelligence reports on environments they only occupied for seconds.
   At eight years old, they are given a test. They have to raise for a while, and then they have to kill a pet (this is to break them of empathy & compassion). Children that are unwilling to kill this pet are removed from the program and moved to an education in administration & support within the Ministry. 
   From age 8-11, the children that advance to the next phase, where the competition for advancement & standing become more pronounced, are treated more like junior initiates than children. A few key points of their education & training during this time are:
      A. Tendon Density Training: Instead of hypertrophy (bulky muscle), the children undergo high-tension isometric training. This builds incredible "wiry" strength and tendon resilience, allowing for explosive speed that exceeds what a larger, more muscular opponent can track visually.
      B. The "Zero-Waste" Movement: They are trained in Systema & Akido, where they learn to never resist force directly; they "fold" and redirect an attacker’s momentum so the enemy’s own weight becomes their undoing.
      C. Hyper-Proprioception: Training involves high-speed obstacle courses in total darkness and sensory-deprivation. This builds a "sixth sense" for spatial awareness, allowing them to track multiple targets in a chaotic fray.
      D. They are given comprehensive sex education and exposed to increasingly graphic sexual situations as observers (such as farm animals and slaves when they think they are unobserved), as well as given access to increasingly explicit pornography within 'hidden' files in their training data.
   After hitting puberty at around age 11 they are given another, more brutal test meant to weed out those who will advance into full initiates. In this test they are forced to rape, torture, and then murder their foster mother in order to advance. If they choose to spare the foster mother, the slave is spared and allowed to re-join the general slave population but the child is removed from the program and put into an education in administration & support within the Ministry, and then eventually become breeding stock for future generations as an adult. 
   From age 11-17 they are given highly advanced combat & perception oriented training in addition to a heavy academic workload. In addition to the classes a normal True Futanari would be expected to take at these ages, they are also taught:
      A. Advanced Weapons Training. They are taught parts of Escrima, Kobudō, and Latigo y Daga that allow the Neurolash to be used as a weapon in multiple configurations.
      B. Neuromuscular Weaponry. They practice drills where they must change the neurolash's configuration mid-swing. This requires extraordinary wrist strength and a "flow state" where the weapon is an extension of their nervous system.
      C. Forensic Psychology & Interrogative "Tuning. They spend hours behind one-way glass in the Processing Facility, watching real-time "Breaking" sessions. They are taught to "tune" their own Voice to match the subject's cortical frequency.
      D. Stress Inoculation & "The Void" Training. They are placed in "The Void" (total darkness and silence) for days at a time, followed by "The Storm" (extreme sensory bombardment). This ensures their mind remains stable even in chaos. They are also subjected to the Neurolash to learn to maintain discipline & a level head even while their own nervous system is being targeted.
   At some point after they turn 17 and the initiates trainers deem her ready, the now young woman will be forced to undergo her final test to become a full member of the Sovereign Hand. When she is deemed ready she is forcibly abducted from her bed in the middle of the night and taken to a brothel in the city, to become a public sex slave for a period of time. While they serve as a sex slave they do so as the lowest class of sex worker, able to be used freely by anyone for just a few credits, while they are blindfolded & restrained. During this time she will be impregnated by a Futanari Breeder before being released and taken back to The Obsidian Citadel where she will complete her training and then give birth to the child, who they are forced to kill after birth (the baby is actually taken to join all the other children in the Obsidian Citadel, but the initiate is made to believe the child was killed so that there would be no chance of seeking a bond with the child later).
   After a short recovery period the final hurdle to becoming a Sister of the Black, which is surviving the DNAM injection that activates the dormant genes for her psionic ability, and if that is survived, the implant of the cybernetics that allow her to control the Neurolash without using controls. Almost 20% of all initiates who undergo the DNAM procedure have a negative reaction and either die, go into a permanent catatonic state, or lose their sanity.
   While captives are in the processing facility, they are subjected to a wide variety of physical, mental, emotional, and genetic testing to determine their quality. The testing reveals the value of five core characteristics Physical Strength (aka Strength Attribute), Agility (aka Dexterity Attribute), Stamina & Toughness (aka Constitution Attribute), IQ (Intelligence Attribute), Will-Power (aka Wisdom Attribute), and Beauty (aka Comeliness Attribute). Each of these characteristics are given a value of 1-10 during testing and additional points are given or subtracted for such things as height, hereditary conditions, and unusual traits that are not easily quantifiable.
   At the end of all the testing they are given a quality rating based on their final score from these tests. The total score needed for each quality rating are as follows:
      Score   Quality Name    Percentage        Example 1     Example 2
      55-60   Superb          0–1%              IQ 190+       Hall of Fame Athlete, Prodigy, Helen of Troy Beauty 
      49-54   Exceptional     3-4%	        IQ 160-189    Professional Athlete, Genius, Supermodel
      42-48   Superior        20%               IQ 120-159    College Athlete, Very Intelligent, Professional Model
      31-41   Common          60%               IQ 90-119     High School Athlete, Normal Intelligence, Attractive
      25-31   Inferior        10%               IQ 70-90      Not Athletic + Dumb + Average Looking
      01-24   Defective       0-1%              IQ below 60   Any hereditary Physical or Mental Disability
   In general a slaves quality rating will determine where they are placed as a slave, with Superb & Exceptional slaves being immediately claimed by the ship captain & ship owner. If there are more than 3 Superb & Exceptional slaves the remainder will go to a private auction open only to Futanari Breeders. If there are less than 3 Superb + Exceptional slaves the captain & owner will pick Superior slaves instead, but all remaining superior slaves are taken to auction where they will be auctioned off according to their overall score, over three separate auctions on four different days. On day 1 the slaves are all presented as a whole, for all potential owners to inspect and make a preliminary bid. At the end of this period the slaves are returned to their cages and their individual bids evaluated. Depending on the bids made and the types of use the bidders make, the slaves will be sorted into either the Day 2 Breeding Slave auction, which is only open to Futanari Breeders, the Day 3 Brothel Slave auction, or the Day 4 Household Slave Auction. Within each auction there is a base price that if a slave is not purchased at, they will move down to the next days auction, and if they cannot be sold above the minimum on Day 4 they are purchased by the state and sent to a work farm.
   While the quality rating based on characteristics may at first seem arbitrary, extensive testing & data analysis by the Ministry of Corrections over the past two decades have refined what was a system of guesswork into a highly accurate system used to determine a slaves likelihood of producing children with above average characteristics themselves, as well as help determine the likelihood of producing True Futanari vs normal males & females. The overall data has shown time and again that the higher quality of the Breeding Slave, the higher quality of the children birthed by them.

Functional Castes & Labor Distribution
   Almost 5% of all slaves become breeding slaves for the Futanari Breeders of the colony. Most of those are owned by Matron Mothers themselves, but many are owned by daughters of the Matron Mothers seeking to establish Houses of their own. If a person were to chose their form of slavery, becoming might seem appealing on the surface as they are basically housed in a harem, with more comforts normally afforded to slaves. The reality of their situation, other than comfort, is that they are generally treated as little more than breeding stock by their owners. While the Futanari Breeder will want their breeding slaves to look & smell nice, their only real use is to bear children for their Futanari Breeder owner, and most are impregnated again almost as soon as they give birth, in a cycle that lasts decades. 
   Those slaves that are purchased to serve in a brothel are actually the slaves with the best life overall. Only around 2% of all slaves become brothel slaves, and their duties can vary wildly. At the bottom of the brothel slaves are the 'public use' slaves, which are stationed in cubicles that allow patrons to use them for a short time for a very low cost. The next tier of brothel slaves are posted in what most would consider a normal brothel, with patrons able to pick their slave and pay for a period of time in a private room, with that room normally being the slaves private room. The highest tier of brothel slaves are the high-priced courtesans, which are slaves that are both especially beautiful & charming. All the high-priced courtesans work at a single club in the city, which functions like a social club & bathhouse in many respects, but with beautiful & charming slaves that can be persuaded to spend time with the patrons for a fee. 
   Household slaves are purchased by Matron Mothers strictly to do normal household duties traditionally done by servants throughout history, such as doing the laundry, cooking & cleaning, doing yardwork and routine maintenance, and occasionally entertaining guests. Others aren't normally as specific in their duties, and the slaves spend almost as much time being bedded as they do doing routine housework. What they all have on common however is they all reside within a private home, within either their own room or a room with 1-3 other slaves.
   Most slaves on Pandora fall into the category of working slaves. These slaves are owned by the state, and generally work in either agriculture (at one of 11 prison-like farms), fishing (at a facility on the bay), or mining (at one of the small colony outposts). The lives of these slaves are strictly monitored & controlled at nearly every moment of every day for their entire life as a slave. While the living arrangements differ a bit in the outpsosts, and only slightly at the fishing facility, the life of the average agriculture slave is a good comparison.
 All slaves are housed in large prison-like complex, with 5 slaves per room. The rooms have bunk beds against 2 walls, and a single larger double bed against the 3rd wall. Each week the room assignments are randomly changed so that it is difficult to form strong bonds and allows the AI that monitors the prisoners to see how the slaves interact with one another with each new grouping. Within the prison-like complex there are a number of jobs that need filled each day for the day-to-day operations of the complex such as laundry, cleaning, and cooking. These jobs are randomly assigned also, but the AI does place weights on certain slaves to perform these jobs based on a number of factors. Typically, everyone is awakened at 5am and have 30 minutes to refresh themselves in communal refreshers. At 5:30 the refreshers stop working and all slaves are moved to the cafeteria for breakfast, socialization, and reviewing of the mornings assigned tasks (assigned by AI). At 6am the cafeteria begins closing and all slaves are moved to their assigned clothing cubicle (if they are working outside, or remain nude if working inside) and then to their assigned work area for the morning (6am-12pm). From 12pm-1pm the slaves are allowed a rest break and are delivered refreshments via drone at a designated break area. Towards the end of the break period they receive their afternoon work assignments and begin working again at their afternoon assignments (1pm-7pm). At 7pm the slaves are instructed to return to the barracks where they remove all of their clothing and store it within their assigned clothing cubicles cleaning slot, and then moved to the communal refreshers. At 7:30pm the cafeteria opens and slaves have 1 hour to eat and socialize or leave the cafeteria to enjoy one of several leisure activities. At 8:30pm the cafeteria closes and all slaves are moved to the leisure activities area, where they will spend time involved with an activity of their choice for another hour. At 9:30pm the slaves are moved to their assigned sleeping area where they must be within by 10pm, when the lights are dimmed and the doors to the rooms are locked for the night.
   There are several things that differ in these complexes from any traditional prisons of the past on Earth that are quite unique and should be pointed out. The first is that while within the indoor areas of the complex no slaves are allowed to wear anything but their collars, which cannot be removed. The second is that there is almost no direct interaction between the slaves and the non-slave employees who work at the complex, who work in a centralized control room or in an adjoining administrative building. The third is that there are no 'guards',  as the controlling AI monitors their location & biometric data at all times and can activate a number of 'corrective measures' in the collar of a slave that steps out of line. Finally, there are no absolute controls over how the slaves can interact with one another as every interaction is used by the controlling AI to analyze the slave in an experiment on human social dynamics. Specifically, the AI is looking for certain behavioral patterns that might warrant a slave being moved to a different setting such as to the combat training slaves if a slave begins to develop an overly aggressive streak toward other slaves.
   While most slaves fall within the previous three categories of slaves, a good number don't fit into the typical roles, including Trained Specialists, Child Developmental Aides, and Dedicated OPFOR Slaves. While slaves are being initially processed some are found to posses especially desirable skills or exceptional traits which makes them valuable to the colony as something other than a laborer or breeding asset. Those with high skills in fields such as Science, Education, Engineering, or The Arts become property of the state and put to work within their field of expertise. While these slaves do have a life more in line with what the average citizen of the colony experiences, they still wear collars linked to the slave control AI, still have their life outside of work controlled, and are still considered slaves.
   Another important group that falls outside the normal categories are the hundreds of women that serve as 'Child Developmental Aides', which are basically foster mothers & nannies for the young children born of Futanari Breeders. These women life in the homes & estates of the Futanari Breeders and care for the children almost as if their own, with little or no input by their mother generally, until the children are old enough to be sent to one of the Boarding schools on the island. These women are generally chosen either during testing if a very high empathy & maternal instinct are indicated, or from the general worker pool if needed.
   The last, and most controversial group of slaves that fall outside of the normal categories are the Dedicated OPFOR Slaves. These slaves are chosen during processing based on having very high strength, toughness, and willpower but do not have the combination of traits to be chosen as a Breeding Slave, Brothel Slave, or Household Slave plus have psychological profiles indicating hyper-aggressive tendencies. Instead of being broken and sent to become Working Slaves, these men are quietly removed from the processing facility and sent to a Ministry of Defense training facility where they are given a choice. They can become members of a dedicated male-only training force used to acclimate the warriors of the colony to fighting against men OR they can return to the processing facility to be broken and sent to a labor facility for the rest of their lives. With the added incentive that in combat training there would be almost zero rules, allowing them to be as brutal as they desire toward their opponents, very few ever say no to this offer.

Life Cycle & Legal Status
   The colony of Themyscira on the colony world of Pandora practices what is commonly known as Chattel Slavery. Under this system slaves are property that can be bought, sold, traded, or seized for debt. The slaves have no legal 'rights' under this system, and there are no contingencies for gaining freedom. With that being said, the Council of Matrons has set out guidelines for how slaves should be treated, and recognize that the slaves are full human beings and should be treated as such. While a specific slaves job & living conditions can vary wildly, they all have several things in common, no matter their location or job:
   (A) All slaves wear a collar given to them by the Ministry of Corrections during processing. This collar is nearly indestructible, is normally sealed, cannot be removed by non-ministry personnel, has sophisticated sensors inside, and have a variety of 'behavioral modification tools' within them that can be used on the slave if needed. While all slaves owned by the state all wear a standard, generic collar, private owners can purchase custom collars for their own slaves.
   (B) Most children born of slaves become slaves themselves. Any child that has a slave for a mother & father, or a slave mother/father with a Freeborn male/female is automatically considered a slave and owned by the state. Children born of a slave mother or father and a Futanari Breeder however are not slaves.
   (C) Slave ownership is not absolute. If a privately owned slave is found to be mistreated beyond the council’s guidelines, or if the slave is required for a State Emergency, the state may seize that slave. In addition, if a Ministry of Corrections officer finds that slaves are being unfairly mistreated by a citizen, they may arrest & prosecute that citizen.
   The Council of Matrons & Ministry of Corrections recognizes that slaves are human beings and cannot be treated as resources to be disposed of when their effectiveness is reduced by aging. Instead, the Ministry has guidelines for a gradual reduction in workload as a slave gets older, with elder slaves being responsible for the welfare & education of slave children much like elderly grandparents. When even this level of work becomes too much for an elderly slave they are relocated to a retirement facility on the island.
   When most slaves are found to be pregnant, they are monitored & evaluated on a regular basis by Freeborn doctors until they hit their third trimester. At that time they are transferred to one of the Nurseries, where their workload is light and there is ready access to medical care. After giving birth these women remain at the nursery for several months with their newborn until the doctors there determine it is safe to send her back to work. The infant children of these women are given over to the care of Child Developmental Aides, or slaves given to taking care of these children until they are around 13-14. Generally this is done in stages, with children moving from one caregiver to another as they progress through stages, and the number of children per caregiver increases at each stage.
   Throughout a child's time in the nurseries they are constantly tested & evaluated using both traditional methods & play-time challenges that will reveal hidden potential. When those children showing promise or potential reach adolescence (around 13-14 years old), they are moved to a special school for slaves that gives them an education more comparable to a Freeborn. Those children who do not show this potential are moved working in the farmland outside of the nurseries in a sort of apprenticeship program until they reach age 18. All slaves go through a slightly modified version of the normal slave processing when they hit age 18, and during this process they are sorted just like incoming new slaves with one major difference. The children that show exceptional promise in a particular field are taken out of processing and transferred to a school on the island as probationary Freeborn, and eventually become citizens if they make it through to the end. Those who are not selected for this honor are processed much like other new incoming slaves and end up in the 18-year old auctions (Breeding Slaves, Brothel Slaves, or Household Slaves) or join the other working slaves.

Geographic Management
   Most slaves live & work in the massive outer zone of the city of Themyscira. Which is protected from the dangers of the planet, but lies outside of the highly protected inner zone where most of the citizens live & work. Within this mostly empty zone are almost a dozen large farms, which have around 350 slaves each, that do the agricultural work for the colony. Over 90% of all the food the average citizen eats is grown in these farms, so the safety of the slaves that work them and continued operation of the farms is of critical importance for the overall colonies well being.
   A significant number, but relatively small proportion of slaves live & work in the inner city. Most that do, are specialists working in one of the districts on behalf of the state, but there are a good number of Brothel Slaves & some Household Slaves as well. While most of the citizens of the city cannot afford slaves of their own or have the space for a slave to live, there are some who do. The barrier to slave ownership for most in the city has to do with housing. While more citizens could afford a personal slave, they live in small 1-bedroom apartments in a housing block, and can't afford a large spacious multi-room townhouse.
   Almost all breeding slaves and many household slaves are located on the island, where the Matron Mothers have their private estates and those who can afford their own slaves often live. These slaves live relatively comfortable lives compared to the slaves within the city, and are often afforded more freedom of movement. Its not uncommon to see slaves at the market, with children at the park, or enjoying a bit of free time at the beach on the island.
   A relatively small number of slaves, chosen for specialized skills or a higher than average survival chance in hostile situations, are chosen to work in one of the remote outposts that serve the colony. Most of the outposts are resource extraction centers involved with mining, gas extraction, or energy production but there are also scientific outposts that could have a permanent slave presence.
